<title>USA: Henkel says Loctite deal clears review.</title>
<headline>Henkel says Loctite deal clears review.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Henkel KGaA said Monday that its pending bid for Loctite Corp has cleared antitrust review by the United States.</p>
<p>The waiting period under that review expired Friday, November 22, the company said.</p>
<p>Its subsidiary, HC Investments, is seeking to acquire Loctite. HC Investments' tender offer is set to expire at 1700 EST/2200 GMT on January 6.  The latest offer to acquire 65 percent of the company, at $57.75 per share, was turned down last week by Loctite.  But Henkel has said it is still interested in pursuing a deal for Loctite.</p>
</text>
